/Title (It is undeniable that water is an important component to life.  In Austin, it is part of daily life. Aside from consumption, numerous individuals swim at Barton Springs, paddle on Lady Bird Lake, and walk the creek trails. Before moving to Austin, however, aquatic environments have been an integral part of my life. Growing up in Laredo, Texas the Rio Grande served as the primary source of water for residents. It also drove the local economic and shaped daily life in the community. Moreover, fishing and kayaking in South Texas were activites my family often enjoyed doing. Thus, conducting an analysis on water quality in Austin felt like a natural way to connect something I grew up with to the place I live now.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 644 0 R
/Next 687 0 R
>>
